1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
You downloaded reinvent_pubchem.prior — that is not choosing a prior.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Tutorial 01 gave you a working env and a real sampled.csv.

3
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Your project is not PubChem. Validity is not relevance.

4
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Prior: frozen pretrained brain. Agent: trainable copy.

5
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Vocabulary lives inside the prior file. We are not training yet.

6
00:02:20,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Same seed, same n, same device — swap only the brain.

7
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Compare ≥2 priors, or prior vs a TL checkpoint.

8
00:03:50,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Measure validity, unique scaffolds, property histograms.

9
00:04:35,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Avoid scaffold collapse. Wrong neighborhood loses later.

10
00:05:20,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Skip PubChem-style priors under domain shift or rare chemotypes.

11
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:30,000
Prefer in-domain priors or a transfer-learning warm start.

12
00:06:30,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Compare, measure, decide — lock the prior before RL.

13
00:07:20,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Full tutorial on the site. Code on GitHub. Link below.
